[h1]Random New World 1.2.0[/h1]

A shared past for the New World: 300 years of simulated history, coherent starting politics, formable countries with real goals, and a new Omerika world type. For EU5 1.4.7.

[h2]🌎 New features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Simulated prehistory (1037–1337).[/b] The 1337 start follows three centuries of unions, wars, treaties, reforms and migration. Choose Calm, Varied or Turbulent history on the World tab. Read each country's story, chronicle, relationships and societal values in the generator, in every official language.
[*][b]Starting politics that hold together.[/b] Countries start with laws and policies the game accepts, treaties within their diplomatic capacity, remembered grievances and goodwill as opinions on the game's own scale, and the start development the game computes.
[*][b]Formable countries with real goals.[/b] Unions, confederations, leagues and commonwealths, a realm of each region and, with fantasy formables, an empire of the New World. Each is a mission, [i]Road to X[/i]. Proclaiming one gives cores on its land. Realms that the history divided can be restored by their heirs, and the AI pursues these goals.
[*][b]Our History as a story.[/b] The decision and the generator tell how each country began, what befell it and where it stands today, instead of a list of dated records. Events of the recorded past let a country press an old claim or renew an old friendship.
[*][b]Omerika.[/b] A familiar New World, reimagined: the general shape of the Americas with entirely new coasts, bays, straits and inland seas. Set how closely the land follows the Americas with Likeness to the Americas. Nothing of the game's map is shipped; it is read from your installation.
[*][b]Keep the real Americas.[/b] Option for Omerika: leave the game's Americas as drawn and generate only their societies, history, laws and formables, in under a minute.
[*][b]Reveal the New World at the start.[/b] Optional setting for multiplayer: the countries that human players choose discover the whole New World when the campaign starts.
[*][b]Inland seas.[/b] Substantial enclosed seas get their own coastal areas and ports; small enclosed waters become lakes instead of stopping generation.
[*][b]Regions laid out and named like the Americas.[/b] Alaska lies in the north-west, the West Coast in the west, Central America in the south, and regions take names from the peoples who live there.
[*][b]Every New World country can settle the frontier.[/b] The game's region gate on [i]Settle the Frontier[/i] no longer locks out about half of the generated countries.
[*][b]A steadier, faster generator.[/b] Continent sketches are drawn side by side and kept, the time left no longer jumps, the queue continues after a failed world, completed worlds appear in the library at once, and switching worlds stays responsive.
[/list]

[h2]🔧 Fixes and improvements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Fixed [i]Create a version[/i] (new peoples or resources) stopping with "The generator stopped". A version of a world made by an earlier algorithm is now refused with the reason, because it could silently give other land.
[*]Fixed countries that opened without a law policy, started over their diplomatic limit, or showed text keys instead of names in decisions, events and formables.
[*]Warns on a world's page when another mod overrides the world's files or when two RNW worlds are enabled; either can leave the New World all Clay.
[*]Fixed the Linux window failing to start on rolling distributions such as Arch.
[*]Total Chaos keeps its name in the library and codes, and can randomize its settings again with the same seed.
[/list]

[quote][b]Updating:[/b] For EU5 1.4.7. Generate a new world for these changes; keep the original world mod for existing saves. World Codes from 1.1.0 can give different worlds in 1.2.0 (algorithm epoch 61), and such worlds cannot be rerolled by part. Use one RNW world at a time and restart EU5 when switching maps.[/quote]

All new texts are translated into the eleven official EU5 languages. Across the Pillars remains optional. Refined Colonization load order: Refined Colonization → generated RNW world mod.

